cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use axiom, or replicate a result through it, please cite it using
  these metadata. Cite the exact commit you ran, not the project in the
  abstract: axiom is a living ledger, and a verdict that names only "axiom"
  is not reproducible. Replace the `commit` field below with the sha you
  actually built.
title: "axiom: an STL-only C++23 mathematics, symbolic-verification, and exact-neural-network library"
abstract: >-
  A from-scratch C++23 library implementing exact arbitrary-precision
  arithmetic, linear algebra, statistics, numerical methods, a symbolic
  (CAS) engine with a three-valued soundness contract, and exact
  fixed-point neural-network inference and integer training. No external
  numerical dependencies: no Eigen, GMP, Boost, BLAS, or torch. Its
  integer NN engine (intbirth) serves as an independent cross-language
  implementation for verifying deterministic training trajectories and
  decodes produced by other runtimes.
type: software
